\section{Parsing and time}{

\code{parse} determines faithful source reading; \code{time} determines local dates
and interval boundaries. Strings below are character scalars.\tabular{ll}{
   Setting \tab Default \cr
   \code{parse$type} \tab \code{"auto"} \cr
   \code{parse$input} \tab \code{"file"} \cr
   \code{parse$encoding} \tab \code{"auto"} \cr
   \code{parse$parser_strict} \tab \code{TRUE} \cr
   \code{time$tz} \tab \code{"Asia/Shanghai"} \cr
}

\itemize{
\item \code{parse$type}: Content selection: \code{auto}, \code{line}, \code{meta}, \code{day}, \code{app}, or \code{legacy}. Auto retains supported mixed line/meta blocks; legacy selects one component.
\item \code{parse$input}: \code{file}, \code{text}, or \code{lines}. Project/cache workflows use file inputs; text/lines are useful with the in-memory readers.
\item \code{parse$encoding}: Automatic decoding or a nonempty source-encoding name, e.g. \code{"UTF-8"}.
\item \code{parse$parser_strict}: Logical: malformed parser structures produce an error condition. Batch continuation is controlled separately by \code{execution$strict}.
\item \code{time$tz}: Valid timezone used for timestamp-derived dates and midnight boundaries.
}
}

\section{Reconstruction and daily tables}{

Numeric durations are milliseconds. Event-type vectors contain Android
UsageEvents codes. Numeric configuration values must be finite and
nonnegative; scalar settings accept one value.\tabular{ll}{
   Setting \tab Default \cr
   \code{reconstruction$include_collection_app} \tab \code{TRUE} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$reconstruct_meta} \tab \code{TRUE} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$meta_pairing} \tab \code{"package"} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$meta_start_event_types} \tab \code{1} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$meta_end_event_types} \tab \code{c(2, 23)} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$merge_meta_episodes} \tab \code{TRUE} \cr
   \code{reconstruction$meta_episode_merge_gap_ms} \tab \code{30000} \cr
   \code{daily$meta_daily_source} \tab \code{"summary"} \cr
}

\itemize{
\item \code{reconstruction$include_collection_app}: Logical: retain \code{com.w.appusage} rows in research-data tables.
\item \code{reconstruction$reconstruct_meta}: Logical: reconstruct pure meta events into episodes. Mixed behavior depends on whether this argument was explicitly supplied; see below.
\item \code{reconstruction$meta_pairing}: Pair by \code{package} or \code{package_class}.
\item \code{reconstruction$meta_start_event_types}: Numeric vector of episode-start event codes.
\item \code{reconstruction$meta_end_event_types}: Numeric vector of episode-end event codes.
\item \code{reconstruction$merge_meta_episodes}: Logical: merge compatible adjacent reconstructed meta episodes.
\item \code{reconstruction$meta_episode_merge_gap_ms}: Maximum merging gap in milliseconds (30 seconds).
\item \code{daily$meta_daily_source}: \code{summary} uses Table 1; \code{episodes} uses reconstructed intervals; \code{both} retains both with source labels. Select one representation when calculating totals.
}

Mixed sources use native line episodes/daily totals and meta Table 2 events
when meta options are omitted. For mixed input, omit \code{meta_daily_source}
and omit \code{reconstruct_meta} or explicitly set the latter to \code{FALSE}.
For explicit meta reconstruction select \code{parse = list(type = "meta")}.
Episode-derived daily modes require reconstruction. The configuration stores
whether those two options were explicitly supplied; editing an expanded
saved list can lose that distinction. Create a new configuration with
\code{\link[=appusage_config]{appusage_config()}}. Old configurations without the explicitness record
retain legacy single-component selection.
